.TH ORG 1 "2026-11-08" "org-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
org \- unified pure-Rust command-line tool for Org-mode files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B org
.RI [ GLOBAL\ OPTIONS ]
.I SUBCOMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.br
.B org
.B \-\-completions
.I SHELL
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B org
lints, formats, queries, mutates, clocks, and exports Org-mode files without requiring Emacs.
It processes files using a single-pass parser and an optional incremental SQLite workspace cache.
All subcommands support human-readable terminal output and machine-readable JSON output for automation pipelines.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B fmt check \fR[\fIPATHS\fR...]
Check Org files for formatting and lint issues without modifying files on disk.
.TP
.B fmt format \fR[\fIPATHS\fR...]
Apply auto-fixable formatting rules (`F001` through `F008`) to Org files in place or on standard input.
.TP
.B query \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Search headings (`search`, `next`, `inbox`, `waiting`, `someday`, `projects`, `stuck`, `blocked`, `deps`, `agenda`, `columns`).
.TP
.B update \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Mutate Org entries (`add-id`, `set-state`, `add-todo`, `add-cookie`, `set-property`, `delete-property`, `set-tags`, `set-scheduled`, `set-deadline`, `add-blocker`, `add-trigger`, `calc`).
.TP
.B clock \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Inspect active clocks (`status`), generate duration and effort variance reports (`report`), or mutate clock entries (`in`, `out`, `cancel`).
.TP
.B export \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Export scheduled and deadline entries to iCalendar (`ical`), RFC 8984 JSCalendar (`jscalendar`), or GitHub Flavored Markdown (`md`).
.TP
.B roam \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Inspect `org-roam` v2 nodes (`node`), incoming backlinks (`backlinks`), outgoing links (`links`), and workspace link graphs (`graph`).
.TP
.B cache \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Inspect (`status`), rebuild (`rebuild`), or remove (`clear`) the incremental SQLite and FTS5 workspace cache.
.TP
.B show \fILOCATOR\fR
Extract a scoped entry subtree or level-0 file node by `OrgLocator` (`id:`, `file::#custom_id`, `file::*Heading`, `file::line`).
.TP
.B refile \fISOURCE\fR \fITARGET\fR
Move an entry subtree across files or under a new parent heading while adjusting outline levels atomically.
.TP
.B mcp \fR[\fB\-\-workspace\fR \fIDIR\fR]
Run the built-in Model Context Protocol (MCP) JSON-RPC 2.0 server over standard input and standard output.
.TP
.B archive \fR[\fIPATHS\fR...]
Move completed (`DONE`) subtrees into their configured archive sibling file (`_archive`).
.TP
.B schema \fR[\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fINAME\fR]
Print or write embedded JSON Schema Draft 2020-12 contracts for `org` JSON outputs.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Bypass the `.cache/org-cache.db` SQLite workspace index and parse `.org` files directly from disk.
.TP
.B \-\-completions \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell completion scripts for `bash`, `zsh`, `fish`, `elvish`, or `powershell` and exit.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Print concise or detailed command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-V\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print the `org` binary version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Operation completed cleanly (`EXIT_OK`).
.TP
.B 1
No query matches found, or lint and format diagnostics were emitted (`EXIT_ISSUES`).
.TP
.B 2
Operational failure such as missing file, parse error, or invalid CLI arguments (`EXIT_ERROR`).
.TP
.B 3
Spreadsheet formula or feature requires Emacs Lisp or full Emacs Calc (`EXIT_REQUIRES_EMACS`).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI color escape sequences in human-readable terminal output when set to any non-empty value.
.TP
.B TERM
Terminal capability type; setting `TERM=dumb` disables ANSI styling and rich box-drawing characters.
.TP
.B ORG_TOOLS_CONFIG
Explicit path to a configuration file overriding `.org-tools.toml` discovery.
.TP
.B VISUAL
Preferred full-screen editor invoked by interactive note capture workflows when set.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Fallback text editor invoked when `VISUAL` is unset during interactive capture workflows.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .org-tools.toml
Project-scoped configuration file discovered in the current working directory or any ancestor directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/org-tools/config.toml
User-level configuration file loaded when no project `.org-tools.toml` file exists.
.TP
.I .cache/org-cache.db
Incremental SQLite WAL and FTS5 workspace index (`WorkspaceCache`) storing parsed nodes, links, and properties.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check formatting and lint rules across a workspace:
.PP
.nf
    org fmt check README.org docs/
.fi
.PP
Query actionable `NEXT` tasks and emit JSON:
.PP
.nf
    org query next notes/ --format json
.fi
.PP
List all embedded JSON Schema Draft 2020-12 contracts:
.PP
.nf
    org schema --list
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.B org-tools.toml(5)
